  "id": "Compound::DB00953 - Gene::3351",
  "verbalization": "Rizatriptan is linked to Htr1b through a shared pathway involving serotonin receptor agonists. Both Rizatriptan and Eletriptan, which are included in the serotonin 1b and 1d receptor agonist classes, bind to Htr1b. This suggests a potential mechanism where Rizatriptan, as part of a broader class of serotonin receptor agonists, interacts with Htr1b through a common biological pathway. The evidence is supported by the lowest common ancestor relationship between Rizatriptan and Eletriptan, which points to Indoles and Serotonin Agonists as shared ontological nodes. The presence of Htr1d, which participates in serotonin binding and is linked to Htr1b, further reinforces the connection. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Rizatriptan in modulating Htr1b activity through serotonin receptor engagement, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
